The constant rank 16 is an observed exact finite property of this coarse relaxation. No structural rank theorem is claimed from it here.

---

## 4. What this rules out

This is a regression against a proof strategy, not evidence for a collapsed source.

It rules out the proposed shortcut

> rotation cell + all uniformly impossible crossings + MI.1 alone

as a complete support-six exclusion: not one of the 388 cells dies under that relaxation.

It does **not** show that any one of the 388 cells contains an exact six-pentagon closure root, much less a globally embedded stopped-train source. The relaxed binary solutions may combine crossing bits whose angle windows have empty simultaneous intersection; they may violate pseudosegment/Jordan constraints; and they may fail the nonlinear vector-closure equations.

The useful consequence is procedural and exact. The crossing walls carry load-bearing information and should not be projected away. The finite endpoint should now be refined in the order

1. exact threshold subdivision by `1<|x_e-x_f|<2`;
2. MI.1 inconsistency elimination;
3. Jordan and stronger pseudosegment realizability tests;
4. nonlinear six-face closure certification/falsification on the residual cells;
5. only then diameter-locking constraints if any global train cells survive.

**Disposition:** exact negative regression. Coarse mod-2 parity is consistent on every one of the 388 collapsed support-six rotation cells, so a complete finite exclusion must retain crossing-threshold information or add stronger geometry. C-II remains open.
